<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Argead dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 7th century–310 BCE</span> · Also known as Argeads, Temenids</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Argead dynasty ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Kingdom of Macedon</a> from around the 7th century BCE until about 310 BCE. Its kings claimed descent from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temenos">Temenos</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argos</a> and through him from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heracles">Heracles</a>, a claim that allowed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-i-of-russia">Alexander I</a> to compete at the Olympic Games. The line included Philip II and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> and ended with the murder of Alexander IV.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/argead-dynasty.jpg" alt="Argead dynasty" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ‍Philly boy92 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vergina_Sun_WIPO.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
